WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:05.338
You might wanna open your eyes,
because our ghost usually writes.

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:06.923
Oh.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:09.426
Relax, we can take the bus back.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:10.969
Great, is GW paying the fare?

00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:15.098
Ha ha ha, don't worry!
We're all mad here.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.224
I'm definitely getting mad.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:21.479
I don't want to say it out loud
because then it might be real.

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:23.815
And I really don't want it
to be real.

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:25.775
I would say no way, 
but then again,

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:29.863
we talk to book characters, so...
anything's possible.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.450
It give me such great happiness
to see you again.

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:36.953
Right, well, now that's out
of the way.

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:40.498
Can we just tell her
that she's from a book?

00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:42.333
No way, it's too weird!

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.752
Couldn't just give us a quiet 
night off,

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:44.586
could you, Ghostwriter?

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:49.758
My grandma wants us to go up to
a wild tiger and... talk to him?

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.259
Not it.

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:53.136
I have a life outside of 
finding missing book characters.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:54.304
Good for you.

00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:56.723
Well, this is the end. 

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.767
At least I made my
bed this morning.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.226
I didn't.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:03.521
Well, GW. Left us a pretty
good cliffhanger.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.608
We’re just, uh...

00:01:08.485 --> 00:01:09.736
Yeah, I got nothing.

00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:10.987
Hello.

00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:12.614
What did you mean by that?

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:16.951
Nothing. I just meant hello 
as in hello.

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:18.745
Well that didn't work.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.163
No kidding, Sherlock.

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:22.082
Take Curtis's bed.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.041
Where am I gonna sleep?

00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:24.959
I don't know. The floor?

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:27.837
I just remembered that 
I have a, um...

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:28.797
A trampoline lesson.

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:29.798
Trampoline lesson!

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.009
Make sure you fit 
into the world of humans.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:33.968
How am I doing?

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:35.804
Could be better.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:37.764
Well played.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.183
I know. I mean thanks.

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:42.685
This is gonna be like 
finding a needle in a haystack.

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:46.231
Hey, thanks Ghostwriter.

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:48.525
There is one thing I 
don't understand.

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:49.525
There's more than one thing

00:01:49.525 --> 00:01:50.525
you can't understand, Joan. 

00:01:50.525 --> 00:01:52.987
You can't understand 
German or French.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:53.987
No.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.616
Uh huh.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.742
You think she's onto us?

00:01:57.742 --> 00:01:58.409
Yeah, Chevon,

00:01:58.409 --> 00:01:59.953
she knows we're 
talking to fictional characters.

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:01.663
It's a little hard to believe.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:04.874
I travel through time
on a transforming pirate ship. 

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:06.709
I'm an expert in 
hard to believe.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.629
Just make sure you 
don't like barricade yourselves

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.214
inside an elevator 
or something. 

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:12.966
That's rule number 
one in horror movies.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.135
This cat is very strange.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.637
Me? Your hair hasn't
been combed in what, 

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:18.637
your whole life?

00:02:20.348 --> 00:02:21.766
Wow. The dogs look great.

00:02:21.766 --> 00:02:23.643
Yeah, no thanks to you. 

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:27.772
My parents will probably 
ground him for the next year. 

00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:29.107
It's like jail for kids.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.860
Sounds like fake science.

00:02:32.443 --> 00:02:34.070
We’re talking to characters 
from a book

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.572
and you're questioning 
fake science?

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:37.740
I'll tell you one thing 
I'm going to do.

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:39.701
Read more books.

00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:41.911
What? I like books now.

